$DIR/test.p:3:21: default parameter values are allowed only in function and method declarations, not in function types, function literals or interface methods
    Default parameter values are allowed only on the parameters of a declared
    function or method. Receivers and results cannot have them, and neither can
    function types, function literals or interface methods, because a call
    through a function value or an interface does not know which function it
    calls, so it could not fill in the defaults.
    (see "Default parameter values" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2201" for a longer explanation)
